1
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,980
The ultimate handicap

2
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,980
Lightly leaping over these hectic times

3
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:37,440
Diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

4
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,420
I wanna time it's a holiday

5
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:45,080
So that I keep wearing
nothing but the latest trends

6
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,240
Because my natural face
is what sells out instantly

7
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:50,980
Let it rain

8
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:58,240
Everybody can do it,
the dreams we set running never stop

9
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,240
Let's set sail again tomorrow, you are

10
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:10,820
Everybody can do it, even if we
stick out a little, it doesn't hurt

11
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:17,800
Holding onto a restless curiosity,
I was reaching higher and stronger

12
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,600
Rules don't scare me.

13
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:36,900
Not that I need to say it again,

14
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:39,420
this month is community outreach month.

15
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:43,240
We aim to be a police force
that the local residents love.

16
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:45,160
When it comes to the citizens,

17
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,320
you are to treat them with extra kindness,
understand?

18
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:49,060
Yes.

19
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:50,600
Yes.

20
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:53,960
Excuse me,
how do I get to the community hall?

21
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:56,940
The community hall is right over there.

22
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:58,120
I'll show you the way.

23
00:01:58,560 --> 00:01:59,620
Let me carry your bags.

24
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,660
I'm so grateful.

25
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:05,360
Chief Ohara, I'll escort the
grandmother to the community hall.

26
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:08,600
Yes, yes,
that is the true image of a police officer!

27
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:13,280
By the way, where's Yotsu?

28
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:16,620
He went out on patrol.

29
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,720
Around 10 yesterday,
together with Honda-san...

30
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:26,760
Uh-oh! The chief's morning
meeting must have already started!

31
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,520
He's going to be furious...

32
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:31,040
We got carried away and went way too far!

33
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:33,700
You're the one who said
you wanted to see Sado!

34
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,600
I thought we'd be back before dawn!

35
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,880
Aaaaaah!

36
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:45,380
Right?

37
00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:47,240
Hey.

38
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:52,140
Let's just blast ahead and not hold back!

39
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,760
What are you going on about,
acting so tough in front of the castle?

40
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:02,740
I'm from Shibamata.

41
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:06,160
This is our turf,
and it's all about violence!

42
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:09,180
We won't let anyone build a
big castle in front of Kameari!

43
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,080
Are you trying to compete with us?

44
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,420
Bring it on!

45
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,880
What a pushover bunch.

46
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:31,920
You're ten years too early to take us on.

47
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,100
W-what? Who are you?

48
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:36,960
I'm Hayato Honda of the Traffic Police Unit.

49
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:38,420
The second Honda.

50
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:42,580
I'm Ryotsu of the Kameari Park police box.

51
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:45,500
If you've got weapons,
I'll take you on anytime.

52
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:51,540
Damn, I'll remember you, Ryotsu!

53
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:58,800
With this, the Chief should
overlook this morning's lateness.

54
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:02,600
After all, we crushed two biker gangs.

55
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:06,360
The best thing to do with that
kind of guy is to knock them flat.

56
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:10,160
That really hurt, you know.

57
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,500
Don't worry,
there'll be at least a cash bonus.

58
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,180
I'd be really happy if
that actually happened.

59
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:20,020
Good morning!
Sorry we're late, really sorry.

60
00:04:21,540 --> 00:04:24,340
Ryotsu, Honda, what on earth did you two do?

61
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:26,840
Just now, a call came in from
the station summoning you!

62
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,520
Heh heh.

63
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:32,080
What! Home confinement, they said?!

64
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:33,500
No, wait, what?

65
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,780
What is going on?!

66
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:38,940
There's no "what" about it! Ryotsu, Honda!

67
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:42,760
Because of you two, complaint calls
have been ringing nonstop since earlier!

68
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,160
I-I'm truly sorry!

69
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,120
My supervisor, Fuyuki Todoki!

70
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:50,380
Whoa, hey! You two, bow your heads already!

71
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:52,880
Wh-wait a minute, please!

72
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:57,100
We beat the living daylights
out of those biker gangs!

73
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:59,940
Why do we have to be punished?!

74
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:04,020
You two dragged ordinary citizens into it!

75
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:04,720
What?

76
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,680
The citizens are furious!

77
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:11,480
Ryotsu, this month is the
community outreach campaign!

78
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:16,540
And yet you go and throw away
the public's trust in an instant!

79
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:19,540
I'm handing down your punishment again!

80
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:25,071
The two of you are confined to your homes for one week,
starting today,

81
00:05:25,121 --> 00:05:29,080
and you will reflect
thoroughly on your past actions.

82
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:29,700
Yes, sir.

83
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:40,600
Home confinement? That's basically the same as getting a vacation,
isn't it?

84
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:44,600
Well then, time to build all those
plastic models I've been putting off.

85
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:51,100
You're so annoying.

86
00:05:51,860 --> 00:05:53,480
Though we didn't get a cash reward.

87
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:55,560
But we got a whole week off!

88
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:57,780
Try to look happier.

89
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:01,640
But I won't be able to
ride my bike the whole time.

90
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:04,680
What am I supposed to do?

91
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:07,440
Just do whatever you like.

92
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,920
Don't you have any hobbies?

93
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:11,980
I don't have any hobbies besides bikes.

94
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,600
Come to think of it, I don't get the
impression Honda does anything either.

95
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:20,520
If you've got nothing to do,
just sleep in your room.

96
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,920
A week goes by in no time.

97
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:47,500
W-what was that?

98
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,560
W-what was all that about?

99
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:55,820
My bike...

100
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:58,120
Gah!

101
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,440
Honda! Where the hell did you pop out from?

102
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,430
My bike...

103
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:05,000
Where's my bike?

104
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:09,200
My bike...

105
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:12,120
My unbuilt model kit!

106
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:15,860
My bike too, in a place like this?

107
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,060
Stop it!

108
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,120
That one I bought from
America by mail order.

109
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,020
Yamaha Virago XV400.

110
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:23,540
It's the real-type model.

111
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,000
It cost me 500 dollars, you know.

112
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:29,760
What a tiny bike.

113
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:34,920
It was a limited release,
and you can't get it anymore.

114
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:38,400
Where's my bike?

115
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,440
Where is it?

116
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:46,860
As long as I'm stuck at home, a fun confinement is a pipe dream.
I've got to do something.

117
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:52,280
Excuse me! Hey...

118
00:07:52,280 --> 00:08:05,720
I've been waiting! I brought all the stuff you asked for, but what's it for?
A hobby to give Honda... a hobby other than bikes

119
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,540
Look at that.

120
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:16,460
Honda-san

121
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:17,680
Are you okay?

122
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:21,880
Why am I in a place like this?

123
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:25,500
Just one day without riding my
bike and look at the state of him.

124
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,600
This is quite a serious injury, isn't it?

125
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:32,620
Honda right now is just like a
salaryman who's just hit retirement.

126
00:08:33,060 --> 00:08:35,240
A man whose whole reason for living was his job,
and then he retires...

127
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:37,560
The moment he loses that reason for living,

128
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:39,680
he just goes totally limp.

129
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:43,280
Especially the type who's devoted only to work,
like the Chief.

130
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:45,160
That kind is the most dangerous.

131
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:47,260
What's that supposed to mean, about me?

132
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:52,380
Chief, why are you here?

133
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:55,280
I'm responsible for supervising you two.

134
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:58,900
I came to make sure you don't cause
any trouble during your suspension.

135
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:01,100
No trouble has happened yet.

136
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,920
Idiots!

137
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:08,000
What do you think you're doing?

138
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:10,920
A ban is a time for reflection.

139
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:14,140
Using it for your hobbies is
completely out of the question.

140
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:16,300
Chief, look at this guy, Reiko -

141
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:18,800
My bike, where's my bike?

142
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:23,700
We haven't eaten a proper
meal since yesterday.

143
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:26,260
At this rate, we'll get sick.

144
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:31,520
We might never be able
to return to work again.

145
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:35,960
Honda is a capable officer of the Hakubai unit,
you know.

146
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:38,960
Naturally,
the Chief will be held responsible too.

147
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:42,140
Expelled from his paradise
of zero managerial ability,

148
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:43,520
he was demoted.

149
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:45,880
He was banished to an obscure,
impoverished village.

150
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:49,320
Among the locals, who are even more
sensitive to rumors than city folk,

151
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:52,340
false rumors flew that he was
"Ohara the subordinate-killer."

152
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:55,860
Unable to endure such a life,
his wife and daughter

153
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:57,320
left home.

154
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,560
With no prospect of promotion,

155
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:02,180
and no hope of returning to Tokyo,

156
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:07,020
he is destined to spend a bleak
old age in loneliness and despair.

157
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:17,060
F-fine, I'll make a special exception.

158
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:21,700
Thank you, sir. That's exactly why
you're such a caring chief, Chief Ohara.

159
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:24,040
You're so good at getting
people to go along with you.

160
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:26,020
That's Ryo-chan's specialty, isn't it.

161
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:29,940
Hobbies are better the
further away they are from work.

162
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:35,440
Coming from someone who neglects work to do nothing but hobbies,
those words are really persuasive.

163
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:36,860
Quiet!

164
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:41,040
For a woman, hobbies should be as far
from motorcycles as possible, I suppose.

165
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:43,480
How about coin collecting?

166
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:44,920
Coin collecting.

167
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:48,060
You can start this one today.

168
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:50,340
To start, let's go with Japanese coins.

169
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:54,460
One-yen, five-yen, ten-yen,
hundred-yen, five-hundred-yen coins.

170
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:58,260
A 1951 ten-yen coin is worth over 100 yen.

171
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:01,244
Shoo-shoo

172
00:11:01,294 --> 00:11:04,679
This one looks like a motorcycle wheel,
doesn't it?

173
00:11:04,729 --> 00:11:06,440
It's perfect for you.

174
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:08,800
Wouldn't a real motorcycle wheel be better?

175
00:11:10,700 --> 00:11:12,359
Chief, that's not allowed, you know.

176
00:11:12,409 --> 00:11:15,040
Saying things that remind
them of motorcycles!

177
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:17,000
S-sorry. That's right.

178
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:19,882
R-right. What about knitting, perhaps?

179
00:11:19,932 --> 00:11:21,960
I'm sure it'd suit Honda-san perfectly.

180
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:22,920
Knitting?

181
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:26,320
That's right.
Making a scarf looks easy enough.

182
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:27,680
A-a scarf?

183
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:30,720
Brown.

184
00:11:31,940 --> 00:11:34,860
Dancing is all the rage these days,
isn't it?

185
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:37,820
Dancing! Folk dancing!

186
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:38,880
Folk!

187
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:41,620
Folk!

188
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:42,840
Y-yeah, yeah.

189
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:45,260
That's right, that's right. Reading!

190
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:49,180
The Trapp Family Story is so moving!

191
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:56,540
Baron, Baron, Baron, Baron!

192
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:59,220
Bikes are the best!

193
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,380
Chief, aren't you already
dancing just by staying silent?

194
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:03,860
S-sorry.

195
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:05,760
Bikeee!

196
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:25,900
Time to go, Mister Yotsu.

197
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:46,600
Good morning, senpai.

198
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:48,180
Are you awake, Ryo-chan?

199
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:50,740
You're here? Just come on in.

200
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,120
Excuse me for intruding.

201
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,840
Wait there, I'm almost done.

202
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:59,100
Were you up all night playing games?

203
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:03,320
I wanted to sleep,
but I couldn't, because of this guy.

204
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:07,380
27631

205
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:10,300
27631

206
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:12,960
27632

207
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,300
27633

208
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:17,660
27634

209
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:20,080
27635

210
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:21,420
27634

211
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:22,980
Ogura-san, what are you doing?

212
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:27,600
If I pop these one per second,

213
00:13:28,660 --> 00:13:33,180
I'll need to pop 431,922 more
before I can ride my bike.

214
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:36,920
Are you planning to keep doing that
the whole time the ban is in effect?

215
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:38,920
Looks like the ban is about to end.

216
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:40,740
Okay, done.

217
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:43,340
Alright, Honda, let's get started.

218
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:45,880
Get started on what?

219
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:49,280
Just look at what Nakagawa
and Reiko are wearing.

220
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:50,860
Tennis, tennis!

221
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:53,020
Tennis is the classic hobby.

222
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:55,300
It's popular with people
of all ages and genders.

223
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:58,760
Plus, Japanese women's
tennis is world-class.

224
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:01,560
These days, you're not really
Japanese unless you play tennis.

225
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:04,580
Yesterday's cultural hobby flopped, so

226
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:06,900
today we're going with a sporty one.

227
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:09,960
I have to head to work soon,
so I can't play with you for very long.

228
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,600
Let's get your bodies moving a little.

229
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,920
It'll refresh both your body and your mind.

230
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:17,700
It's fine, I'm doing this.

231
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:20,560
If you keep doing that,
you'll only end up feeling negative.

232
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:21,800
Now, wait!

233
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:24,640
No way, if I play tennis I'll wreck my body!

234
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:28,540
What wimpy nonsense is a biker talking? Hey!

235
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:30,120
Is Ryotsu here!

236
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:33,400
Ryotsu, Honda! You two...

237
00:14:33,450 --> 00:14:35,600
You're fired, fired! I'm showing no mercy!

238
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:36,680
What, wh-what!?

239
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:37,900
Fired...

240
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:40,180
W-what happened, Chief?

241
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:42,360
What happened? You may well ask!

242
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:45,250
Even though these two
are under home confinement,

243
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:47,500
they went on a rampage
in Kanagawa last night!

244
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:54,360
Around 2 a.m. last night, a pair calling themselves Honda and Ryotsu
of the Kameari Kōen-mae police box

245
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:56,080
appeared on Kanagawa Street.

246
00:14:56,920 --> 00:15:00,420
Claiming to be enforcing the law,
they harmed many cars!

247
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:02,340
Honda and Ryotsu went on
a street-attacking spree

248
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:04,300
and even called in the police officers.

249
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:08,740
Crowds have swarmed the area,
and it's turned into a huge commotion.

250
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:11,520
That wasn't us, you know.

251
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:12,760
Silence.

252
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,800
So are you saying there
are fakes of you two?

253
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:20,260
We know it was you two for certain,
based on the eyewitness testimony.

254
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:20,960
No way.

255
00:15:22,060 --> 00:15:24,340
The official disciplinary decision
will come out within a few days, but

256
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:28,880
Honda will probably have his
license revoked and be dismissed.

257
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,320
Dismissed.

258
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:35,420
Ryotsu is definitely getting dismissed too.

259
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:39,960
Until a conclusion is reached,
stay at home and behave yourselves.

260
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:42,420
Understand? Under no
circumstances are you to go outside.

261
00:15:45,020 --> 00:15:46,790
Setting Ryo-chan aside,

262
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:51,240
I can't believe Honda would ignore his home
confinement and go on a rampage outside.

263
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:52,740
Hm?

264
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:56,458
True, setting aside senpai,
in Honda's case,

265
00:15:56,508 --> 00:16:01,280
it's more natural to think someone
is using his name and causing trouble.

266
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,925
Hey, Honda, you believe me, right?

267
00:16:02,975 --> 00:16:06,140
So you don't trust me at all?

268
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:08,285
N-no, that's not it at all.

269
00:16:08,335 --> 00:16:12,200
Given how Honda was acting
he was here just a moment ago.

270
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:16,980
Aaaaah! Honda!

271
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:19,820
Don't tell me he...

272
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:27,940
Honda, Nakagawa, here's Lego!

273
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:30,920
Honda-san!

274
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:32,440
Aaaaaah!

275
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:42,460
Honda

276
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:47,940
Idiot, stop! What good will dying do?

277
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:50,120
What are you doing?

278
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:53,760
Honda, please calm down.

279
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:56,260
The truth will come out eventually,

280
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:58,000
and your house arrest will be lifted.

281
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,880
That's right, hold on, Honda.

282
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:04,180
If you die, your father and your mom

283
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:06,780
and your little sister Ibu-chan
and little brother Kadoki...

284
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:10,000
And Grandpa and everyone
at Kōki will be heartbroken!

285
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:12,420
What are you talking about?

286
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:15,940
I was just looking at the motorcycles.

287
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,880
Don't go doing something so foolish!

288
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:24,760
Senpai!

289
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:25,540
Ryo-chan!

290
00:17:25,980 --> 00:17:32,560
Ow!

291
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:34,380
Can't you move, Ryo-chan?

292
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:38,780
Honestly, for us it was just a scratch.

293
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:41,760
For an ordinary person, even with good luck,
it would be a serious injury.

294
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:44,880
If this keeps up, I'll really get angry.

295
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:47,720
Yes, that's quite likely.

296
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:49,880
We don't have a moment to lose.

297
00:17:50,340 --> 00:17:52,400
Let's catch the real culprit quickly.

298
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:54,200
I'll help too.

299
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:57,600
Ryo-chan, who'd probably get by even after quitting the police,
is one thing...

300
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:59,460
but Honda-san is so pitiful.

301
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:02,800
Yes, senpai aside, Honda-san is...

302
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:23,500
Looks like the police are in an uproar.

303
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:27,120
If you cause trouble today,
you're definitely getting fired, Honda.

304
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,860
Oops, right, I'm Honda now.

305
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,920
Let's go, my lord.

306
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:32,500
Yeah.

307
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:45,480
Hey, hey, make way!

308
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:47,260
Make way for the mighty Honda!

309
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:49,820
There's the lord of the domain!

310
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:54,000
H-hey, what do you think you're doing?!

311
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,600
I absolutely hate red horses!

312
00:18:56,600 --> 00:18:59,500
Doing whatever you want violates the rules,
so pay 50,000 yen!

313
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:00,660
N-no way!

314
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:02,480
Shut up!

315
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:03,720
Don't exist!

316
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:05,720
This is a late-model Honda!

317
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,760
Behold, the lord of the first domain!

318
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:09,300
He's the real deal!

319
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:10,440
Come out here!

320
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:12,600
Noooo!

321
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:16,660
What?!

322
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:27,060
Don't let them get away!

323
00:19:27,060 --> 00:19:28,900
Senpai, you'll regret this.

324
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:32,141
Let's go,

325
00:19:32,191 --> 00:19:34,660
Honda.

326
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,400
But how are we supposed to
get down from Honda's place?

327
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:43,760
Hey, quit your whining and just hop on already,
come on.

328
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:48,660
You fakes, prepare yourselves!

329
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:11,920
What?

330
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:12,460
W-what?

331
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:20,420
How dare you use our names!

332
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:22,220
You're not getting off easy!

333
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:23,860
It's the real ones!

334
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:24,940
No way I'm getting caught!

335
00:20:29,820 --> 00:20:30,880
Don't let them escape, no matter what!

336
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:31,960
Give up already!

337
00:20:46,560 --> 00:20:47,420
Get back here!

338
00:21:18,540 --> 00:21:20,380
Whoa! Out of the way, out of the way!

339
00:21:21,740 --> 00:21:23,320
Don't come near me!

340
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,980
That'll be 736 yen.

341
00:21:37,380 --> 00:21:38,340
Welcome!

342
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:40,260
Get back here!

343
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:51,520
Show your true colors, you!

344
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:08,480
You lot...

345
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:11,300
Probably the head of Violence Special!

346
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:13,880
The one behind is the Sigma leader, man.

347
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:15,540
We're busted!

348
00:22:16,260 --> 00:22:16,940
What is this?

349
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:21,420
So this is the impostor's doing, holding
a grudge over being crushed by those two!

350
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,360
W-what is it?!

351
00:22:25,360 --> 00:22:26,280
Yoisho! Shields!

352
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:28,360
Wow, a demon god!

353
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:32,520
Damn it, if I get fired because of Ryotsu,
I'll make him pay!

354
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,700
How far are you going to chase
us before you're satisfied?!

355
00:22:43,760 --> 00:22:44,500
Emera!

356
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:47,560
You went and did something
you're not supposed to do!

357
00:22:48,580 --> 00:22:49,960
You've made me angry!

358
00:22:52,300 --> 00:22:54,100
Watch yourself from now on, kid!

359
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:18,960
We did it! We did it!

360
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:21,260
This will prove our innocence!

361
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:23,800
We can ride our bikes openly again!

362
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:40,240
Chief!

363
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,900
So it really was you two after all!

364
00:23:46,060 --> 00:23:47,820
There's a deep reason for this...

365
00:23:49,500 --> 00:23:50,840
I've had enough!

366
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:52,680
You're fired! Absolutely fired!

367
00:24:04,080 --> 00:24:06,380
Nakagawa, put more emotion into your acting!

368
00:24:06,380 --> 00:24:09,260
This is supposed to be the scene
where you reunite with your mother,

369
00:24:09,260 --> 00:24:11,260
whom you were separated from long ago,
in a tearful reunion!

370
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:14,720
This is sure to boost the ratings.

371
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:16,020
Cameras on standby, OK.

372
00:24:16,440 --> 00:24:17,740
Alright, we're going live.

373
00:24:18,820 --> 00:24:20,920
We'll go for ratings next time.

374
00:24:21,300 --> 00:24:22,020
Take care of it, okay.

375
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:37,760
Even if you stop the clocks,
time keeps moving on.

376
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:48,000
Don't scowl, laugh it off and keep living.

377
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:57,920
Even if today is rainy,

378
00:24:57,920 --> 00:25:03,480
tomorrow will be sunny.

379
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye.

380
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,880
Unpleasant things, farewell.

381
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:21,480
Oh yeah, let's try living as we please.

382
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:23,980
Good things will come.

383
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:30,280
Outside the door, the sun is calling you.

384
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

